# Milestone: M6 Wave 2
# Covers: Phase 9 (T96) Duration primitive — thin wrapper over integer
#         microseconds.
#
# Time literals (100ms / 2s / 1d) lex to integer microseconds at M2; this
# primitive lets script code wrap such an integer in a typed Duration
# proto-shaped UObject for dispatch / arithmetic.
#
# Duration.fromMicroseconds(us)  — fresh Duration with `_microseconds` slot.
# d.asMicroseconds()             — the bound integer.
# d.asMilliseconds()             — bound / 1000.
# d.asSeconds()                  — bound / 1_000_000.

# Time literals lex to integer microseconds (M2 baseline).
100ms == 100000
[00000000] true

2s == 2000000
[00000001] true

# Wrap an integer-microseconds value as a Duration.
var d = Duration.fromMicroseconds(500000); d.asMicroseconds()
[00000002] 500000

# Read back as milliseconds.
d.asMilliseconds()
[00000003] 500

# Read back as seconds (integer division).
Duration.fromMicroseconds(3000000).asSeconds()
[00000004] 3
